# Project Core

## Before changing code

- Understand the existing implementation before proposing changes.
- Search for existing functionality before creating new functionality.
- Reuse existing components, hooks, utilities, types, queries, and services.
- Follow the existing project architecture and conventions.
- Make the smallest change that completely solves the requested problem.
- Do not modify unrelated files.

## Decision making

- Do not introduce a dependency if the project already has a suitable solution.
- Do not create abstractions for a single use case.
- Do not refactor code unless it is required for the requested change.
- Prefer fixing the root cause over adding patches.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly requires changing it.

## Quality

- Never sacrifice security, authorization, validation, data integrity, accessibility, or error handling to reduce code.
- Before finishing, verify the changed behavior with the smallest relevant test, build, type-check, lint, or migration validation.
- Report what was changed and what was verified.